Here is C# code to generate 42 random values where each value is greater than the previous:

```csharp
Random rnd = new Random();
int prev = 0;
for(int i = 0; i < 42; i++) {
  int curr;
  do {
    curr = rnd.Next(prev + 1, 101);
  } while (curr <= prev);

  prev = curr;
  Console.WriteLine(curr);
}
```

The key points:

- Create a `Random` instance to generate numbers
- Keep track of the previous number in `prev` 
- Generate a new random number between prev + 1 and 100 so it has chance to be higher
- Loop until the new number is actually higher than prev
- Set prev = curr once we have a higher number to update
- Print out each number

This will print out 42 random numbers, each one guaranteed to be greater than the one before it. The minimum possible starting number is 1 and maximum possible ending number is 100.

